{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `8ae6db56`: as you recommend. The one refresh command\nupdates the hashes and `syncCommit` together, and only that route\nreads Git. The pins check starts no subprocess.\n\nOne condition: the refresh refuses when a mapped file differs from\nits bytes at the commit that it records. So each recorded hash is\nthe hash of a file at `syncCommit`, and a reader can check the pair\nwith Git alone.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}